<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bidouze</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bidouze is a river of the French Basque Country, about 80 kilometres long, a left tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adour">Adour</a>. It rises in the foothills of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> near the border of Soule and Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> and flows north past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidache">Bidache</a> to join the Adour.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bidouze.jpg" alt="Bidouze" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iñaki LL · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bidaxune_-_Biduze_ibaia_(2022)_7.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
